{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310588,"nonce":"tAf8DpHLANOh8hZTall6+8301fk=","title":"FIXED 1fb630eb: Dynamic == Dynamic compared BOX ADDRESSES for function parameters, so equals(a,b) was always false. Fixed at runtime via ...","message":"`a == b` on two `Dynamic` values compiled to a comparison of the BOX ADDRESSES\nwhenever they arrived as FUNCTION PARAMETERS. `a == a` was true, two distinct\nboxes holding 42 were false — so any `equals(a, b)` helper silently returned\nfalse for every call. Found when a test helper printed \"got 42 want 42\" as a\nFAILURE on nine assertions.\n\nRoot cause: the value-aware Dynamic path in `hir_to_mir.rs` decides \"is this\noperand boxed\" for a Variable purely from `boxed_dynamic_symbols`, which is\npopulated from Let/Assign. A parameter is boxed by the CALLER and never\nrecorded.\n\nWidening the check to \"register type is not a concrete scalar\" **breaks\nArray.sort**. A parameter holding a genuine box and an untyped lambda parameter\nholding a RAW i64 are BOTH untracked `Ptr(Void)` — instrumented and confirmed\nidentical. So `function(a, b) return a - b` gets its raw integers unboxed as\nDynamicValue* → SIGSEGV in `test_array_methods`. The register type carries NO\nsignal here.\n\nDecide at RUN time, where the information exists. Eq/Ne on two pointer-shaped\nDynamic operands call `haxe_dynamic_equals` (runtime/src/type_system.rs), which\nvalidates each side before dereferencing — aligned, above the first page, tag in\nthe plausibility window (`tid \u003c= TYPE_ARRAY || tid \u003e 100`, same window the\ndynamic coercions use) — and falls back to pointer identity when a side is not a\nbox. **Arithmetic is deliberately untouched**; only Eq/Ne route through it.\n\nAlso fixes what the both-boxed path got wrong even when it ran: it unboxed to\nf64 unconditionally, reading a string as a double and unable to tell `1` from\n`\"1\"`. Now Int/Float compare numerically across types, Bool and String by value,\neverything else by reference, two nulls equal.\n\nTest: `compiler/tests/haxe/test_dynamic_equality.hx` (17 cases, both backends).\n\nSame family as [[feedback_fqn_first_resolution]] in spirit: a decision made from\na proxy (register shape / bare name) instead of from the declaration or the\nvalue itself. Cross-module Dynamic reflection is a separate open issue —\n[[bugs_cross_module_dynamic_object_reflection]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_dynamic_equality_compared_box_addresses` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}